      <div class="rx-photo">{% image "hiw2-quote-moving-boxes.jpg", "Boxes being packed for a move into a care home" %}<div class="rx-tag">from<strong>&pound;{{ (site.packages | findByKey("bronze")).price | gbp }}</strong>packing and removals</div></div>
      <div class="rx-copy">
        <span class="gd-eyebrow" style="text-align:left">Care home move</span>
        <h2>The practical side of a move into a <em>care home</em></h2>
        <p class="rx-sub">Moving into a care home is an emotional step for the person and for their family. The practical work is often what families find hardest to fit in around visits, work and everything else. We take that on, at a gentle pace and with the family involved as much as they wish.</p>
        <ul class="rx-points"><li><i class="fas fa-clipboard-list" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Choosing what comes</h3><p>A care home room is much smaller than a family home. We help decide what fits and matters most, so the room feels familiar from the first day.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-box-open" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Packed with care</h3><p>Every box is labelled by destination, with medication, important papers and everyday essentials kept easy to reach.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-truck" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>A fully insured removal</h3><p>Insured against loss or damage in transit, with the cover set out in your service agreement before the move begins.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-home" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Setting up the new room</h3><p>Photographs, bedding, a favourite chair and familiar objects put in place, so the room is ready when your relative arrives. The previous home can then be sorted later, without time pressure.</p></li></ul>
        <p class="rx-where">What is included depends on the package you choose. We help with the practical move only. The decision to move, the choice of home and any care or funding questions are for the person, their family and their care and medical professionals.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gd-sec grey">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="gd-head"><span class="gd-eyebrow">How a care home move runs</span><h2>From first call to <em>settled in</em></h2></div>
    <ol class="rx-line" style="--n:4"><li><span class="gd-num">1</span><h3>Plan it</h3><p>A Discovery Consultation, from &pound;{{ (site.packages | findByKey("discovery")).price | gbp }}, gives you a plan, timeline and budget in an hour, in person or by phone.</p></li><li><span class="gd-num">2</span><h3>Sort what comes</h3><p>We agree with you what goes into the room and what stays for later, item by item and with your agreement.</p></li><li><span class="gd-num">3</span><h3>Pack and move</h3><p>Careful packing, then an insured removal on a day that suits your relative and the home.</p></li><li><span class="gd-num">4</span><h3>Settle in</h3><p>The new room set up with familiar things. Sorting the old home can wait until the family is ready.</p></li></ol>
    <p class="rx-cap">Tell us if the move is urgent. We work to shorter timescales where we can, though the more notice we have, the gentler it can be.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gd-sec">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="gd-head"><span class="gd-eyebrow">What to take</span><h2>Making a small room feel <em>like home</em></h2></div>
    <div class="gd-rows">
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Ask the home first</h3><p>Many care homes provide a bed and some furniture, and have rules about fire safety. Check what the home provides and what you may bring before you pack anything large.</p></div>
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Electrical items and PAT testing</h3><p>Many homes require electrical items such as lamps, radios, TVs and electric blankets to pass a PAT (portable appliance) safety test before they can be plugged in. Ask whether the home tests them or expects you to arrange it, and consider battery-powered radios or clocks to use in the meantime.</p></div>
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Start with what is personal</h3><p>Photographs, a favourite blanket or cushion, a clock, books, a small piece of furniture and familiar ornaments do the most to make a room feel like theirs.</p></div>
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Label everything</h3><p>Clothes and personal items are usually best labelled with the person&rsquo;s name. Ask the home whether it has its own labelling arrangements.</p></div>
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Keep the rest for later</h3><p>The family home does not need emptying before the move. If a sale or a bereavement follows, our guide to <a href="/blog/moving-after-probate-clearing-a-loved-ones-home/">moving after probate and clearing a loved one&rsquo;s home</a> explains the next steps.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

